<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">High Court of Australia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The High Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> is the highest court of the Commonwealth of Australia, provided for in the federal constitution of 1901 and established in 1903. It interprets the constitution, settles disputes between the Commonwealth and the states and hears final appeals. Appeals from it to the Privy Council in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> were ended by 1986, and the court has sat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canberra">Canberra</a> since 1980.</p></div>
